message: "If you use this model in teaching, research or a publication, please cite it as below."
title: "ESP32-C3 in Logisim: a gate-level ESP32-C3 microcontroller for Logisim Evolution"
abstract: >-
  A complete ESP32-C3 microcontroller built as a digital logic circuit for Logisim Evolution:
  a multicycle RISC-V RV32IMC CPU with CSRs and interrupts, system bus, boot ROM, FLASH, SRAM and
  the digital peripherals (GPIO with IO MUX, UART, SYSTIMER, timer groups with watchdogs, LEDC PWM,
  SPI, I2C, interrupt matrix), following the memory map of the real chip. It runs programs written
  in Arduino and ESP-IDF style through a bundled SDK, includes a version whose ALU adder is built
  from 896 CMOS transistors, and passes the official riscv-tests suite (rv32ui, rv32um, rv32uc).
